{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-translate-brevity-translation-output-lengths","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-translate-brevity-translation-output-lengths/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:04:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:56:18+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a\u0026nbsp;neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today we are launching brevity, a new Amazon Translate feature customers can use to shorten translation lengths compared to Translate’s default output. Brevity customization reduces the cost and effort required to manually adjust lengths of machine translated output.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers have to translate content such as product headings, image captions, and video subtitles that have constraints on translation output length. For such use cases, customers can now use this brevity feature to reduce most output lengths while conveying the same message. For example, consider translating the following image caption from Spanish to English: “El perro corrió tras de la bola tremendamente grande.” A customer with a 40-character caption size limit will want to shorten the 46-character default translation: “The dog ran after the tremendously large ball.” Activating brevity reduces the output to 32-characters, \u0026quot;The dog ran after the huge ball.\u0026quot; In this case, brevity automatically shortens the translation and meets the customer need while preserving the underlying message.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe brevity feature is now available with real-time text translation in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Translate is available, and for a specific subset of Amazon Translate supported language pairs. To learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/customizing-translations-brevity.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation on translation customization with brevity\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-01T17:06:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-translate-brevity-translation-output-lengths/","postDateTime":"2023-11-01T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate introduces brevity customization to reduce translation output lengths","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a\u0026nbsp;neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today we are launching brevity, a new Amazon Translate feature customers can use to shorten translation lengths compared to Translate’s default output. Brevity customization reduces the cost and effort required to manually adjust lengths of machine translated output.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-amazon-translate-language-detection-document-translation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-translate-language-detection-document-translation/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are enabling language detection for real time document translation. Customers can now automatically detect the source document\u0027s dominant language leveraging \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/comprehend/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Comprehend’s\u003c/a\u003e language detection API.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSynchronous document translation supports language pairs with English as either the source or the target language, and document sizes up to 100KB. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/sync.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003esynchronous document translation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-04T17:04:07Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-translate-language-detection-document-translation/","postDateTime":"2023-08-04T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate enables language detection for real time document translation ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are enabling language detection for real time document translation. Customers can now automatically detect the source document\u0027s dominant language leveraging \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/comprehend.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Comprehend’s\u003c/a\u003e language detection API.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-07-amazon-translate-real-time-translation-docx-files","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/07/amazon-translate-real-time-translation-docx-files/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:56:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are enabling real time translation of Docx files. With this launch, Real Time Document Translation can synchronously translate HTML, TXT and Docx files, while preserving the source document format. Customers can use the API via SDK, CLI, or the AWS management console to submit a translation request and receive the document back with source formatting intact.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature will now support language pairs with English as either the source or the target language, and document sizes up to 100KB. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/sync.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003esynchronous document translation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-07-19T21:20:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/07/amazon-translate-real-time-translation-docx-files/","postDateTime":"2023-07-19T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate enables real time translation of Docx files","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are enabling real time translation of Docx files. With this launch, Real Time Document Translation can synchronously translate HTML, TXT and Docx files, while preserving the source document format. Customers can use the API via SDK, CLI, or the AWS management console to submit a translation request and receive the document back with source formatting intact.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-amazon-translate-enhances-terminology-feature","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-translate-enhances-terminology-feature/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:59:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today we are announcing enhancements to the custom terminology feature that will improve translation fluency and accuracy. The enhancement creates contextually appropriate versions of matching terms to generate translations of higher quality. For example, if the matching term is singular, but the sentence requires a plural, the new version automatically performs this conversion. This enhancement also allows customers to expand the application of their term bases to wider set of translations, as illustrated in the example below.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eLet’s say a customer adds the English term “sign out” paired with the Spanish target translation “finalizar sesión” to their custom terminology file. With the new update, translations that require other forms of the phrase “finalizar sesión” can also be updated without compromising fluency. The sentence, “I asked him to sign out of his account” can seamlessly be translated to “Le pedí que finalizara sesión en su cuenta”, and not the grammatically incorrect “Le pedí que finalizar sesión en su cuenta”. This update removes the need for customers to have to add separate terminology entries with variations such as “finalizar sesión” and “finalizara sesión”.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWe recommend the use of Custom Terminology for all languages except Russian. This feature is available in all regions where Amazon Translate is available. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/how-custom-terminology.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecustom terminology\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-06-30T20:38:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-translate-enhances-terminology-feature/","postDateTime":"2023-06-30T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate enhances its custom terminology feature","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today we are announcing enhancements to the custom terminology feature that will improve translation fluency and accuracy. The enhancement creates contextually appropriate versions of matching terms to generate translations of higher quality. For example, if the matching term is singular, but the sentence requires a plural, the new version automatically performs this conversion. This enhancement also allows customers to expand the application of their term bases to wider set of translations, as illustrated in the example below.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-05-amazon-translate-document-translation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-translate-document-translation/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:01:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:32:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are announcing the general availability of real time document translation feature that allows customers to translate HTML and Text documents in real time. Until today, to translate documents in real time, customers had to extract the text, translate the text into the target language, and post-process the translated text to convert it into the original file format. With the new real time document translation feature there is no need for any pre-processing or post-processing steps. Customers can use APIs or the AWS console to submit a translation request and receive documents back with source formatting intact.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAt launch this feature will support HTML and Text file formats, with English as the source or target language, and document size up to 100KB. This feature is available in 16 commercial AWS regions at launch. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation on\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/sync-api.html#sync-api-document\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003esynchronous document translation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-05-25T22:39:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-translate-document-translation/","postDateTime":"2023-05-24T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate launches real time document translation","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are announcing the general availability of real time document translation feature that allows customers to translate HTML and Text documents in real time. Until today, to translate documents in real time, customers had to extract the text, translate the text into the target language, and post-process the translated text to convert it into the original file format. With the new real time document translation feature there is no need for any pre-processing or post-processing steps. Customers can use APIs or the AWS console to submit a translation request and receive documents back with source formatting intact.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-amazon-translate-batch-translation-eight-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-translate-batch-translation-eight-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:56:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:29:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate asynchronous Batch Translation is now available in eight additional regions - US West (Northern California), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Paris) and Europe (Stockholm). With this expansion, Amazon Translate asynchronous Batch Translation is supported in 15 regions. Now, AWS customers can reach a wider set of users in many geographies that are increasingly expecting to consume media and interact with organizations in the language of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith asynchronous Batch Translation, customers can translate a large collection of documents stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) bucket. Asynchronous batch operations are particularly useful for translating large collection of documents with one API call, when the application doesn\u0027t need a real-time response. Our asynchronous Batch Translation service accepts a batch of up to 5 GB in size per API call with each document not exceeding 20 MB in size and the number of documents in the S3 bucket folder not exceeding 1 million per batch. Refer to our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is-limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGuidelines and Limits\u003c/a\u003e for more details.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor a full list of regions Amazon Translate supports, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regional Services List\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003easynchronous batch translation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-03-29T16:58:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-translate-batch-translation-eight-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-03-29T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate launches Batch Translation in eight additional regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate asynchronous Batch Translation is now available in eight additional regions - US West (Northern California), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Paris) and Europe (Stockholm). With this expansion, Amazon Translate asynchronous Batch Translation is supported in 15 regions. Now, AWS customers can reach a wider set of users in many geographies that are increasingly expecting to consume media and interact with organizations in the language of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-translate-doubles-synchronous-real-time-text-translation-limits","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-translate-doubles-synchronous-real-time-text-translation-limits/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:40:14+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Customers use TranslateText API for real time text string translations to support use cases like chat translation. Earlier, the TranslateText API had a size limit of 5,000 bytes for translation requests. Starting today, customers can now use the TranslateText API  for real time translation requests up to 10,000 bytes.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all commercial AWS regions wherever synchronous translation service is available. To learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/APIReference/API_TranslateText.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation on TranslateText API\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-29T19:10:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-translate-doubles-synchronous-real-time-text-translation-limits/","postDateTime":"2022-12-29T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate doubles its synchronous real-time text translation limits to 10,000 bytes","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Customers use TranslateText API for real time text string translations to support use cases like chat translation. Earlier, the TranslateText API had a size limit of 5,000 bytes for translation requests. Starting today, customers can now use the TranslateText API  for real time translation requests up to 10,000 bytes.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-translate-support-files-stored-s3-nested-folders","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-translate-support-files-stored-s3-nested-folders/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:47:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, Amazon Translate launches support for translation of files stored in nested S3 folders.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAll files under the input S3 folder and its sub-folders will be validated and translated via Amazon Translate’s asynchronous batch translation service. Customers can now preserve their folder hierarchy when they wish to use Amazon Translate and no longer need to use a flat folder structure for their translation jobs. This update is compatible with all the other asynchronous batch translation features. This feature will not support files stored in the root S3 folder.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for asynchronous batch translation of files stored in nested S3 folder structure is available in all commercial AWS regions wherever asynchronous batch translation service  is available. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation\u0026nbsp;on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003easynchronous batch translation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-13T18:14:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-translate-support-files-stored-s3-nested-folders/","postDateTime":"2022-12-13T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate enables support for files stored in S3 nested folders","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, Amazon Translate launches support for translation of files stored in nested S3 folders.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-translate-language-detection-support-batch-translation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-translate-language-detection-support-batch-translation/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:29:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Amazon Translate now supports  language detection of input files for batch translations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon batch translation service will allow customers to translate multiple languages files in one translation job by detecting the dominated source language in each file. Customers can now mix multiple languages files in one S3 bucket and create one job without specifying the source language. This feature samples first 1,000 characters in each file and detects the dominat language as the source language and translates each file to the specified target language by leveraging Amazon Comprehend’s language detection API.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all commercial AWS regions wherever asynchronous batch translation service  is available. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003easynchronous batch translation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-12T19:59:11Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-translate-language-detection-support-batch-translation/","postDateTime":"2022-12-12T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate enables language detection support for batch translation","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Amazon Translate now supports  language detection of input files for batch translations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-translate-tagging-support-parallel-data-custom-terminology","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-translate-tagging-support-parallel-data-custom-terminology/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:56:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:24:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation.\u0026nbsp;Today, we are launching support of tagging for custom terminology and parallel data resources and then allow/restrict access on them based on the tags.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTagging allows customers to assign metadata to their AWS resources. Each tag is a simple label consisting of a customer-defined key and an optional value that can make it easier to manage, search for, and filter resources by purpose, owner, environment, or other criteria. AWS tags can be used for many purposes such as automation, operations support, and attribute based access control. Attribute Based Access Control allows finer grained control than API level and more dynamic control than resource-based access control. Customers can create IAM policies that allow or disallow a Translate operation based on tags provided in the request (request-tags) and tags on the resource that is being operated on (resource-tags).\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTagging is now available for custom terminology and parallel data resources in commercial AWS regions where Amazon Translate is available. To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/tagging.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eon tagging translate resources\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-18T23:12:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-translate-tagging-support-parallel-data-custom-terminology/","postDateTime":"2022-11-18T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Enables Tagging Support for Parallel Data and Custom Terminology","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation.\u0026nbsp;Today, we are launching support of tagging for custom terminology and parallel data resources and then allow/restrict access on them based on the tags.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-10-amazon-translate-formality-customization-support-dutch-korean-mexican-spanish","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/amazon-translate-formality-customization-support-dutch-korean-mexican-spanish/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:27:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are adding formality customization support for Dutch, Korean, and Mexican Spanish. We are also adding support for asynchronous batch translation. Now you can customize the formality of your translated output to suit your communication needs. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Translate’s formality customization, customers have three options - default, formal and informal - to control the level of formality in the output. The default option does not change the formality of the neural machine translation output. The formal option has a higher level of formality compared to the default option, and can be used by customers in Insurance and Healthcare industry who need highly formal translations. The informal option has a lower level of formality, and can be used by customers in Gaming and Social Media who prefer informal translations\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFormality customization is now available in both the real-time and asynchronous batch operations in commercial \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Translate is available. For step-by-step instructions on how to customize the formality of your translation output, read our blog “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/control-formality-in-machine-translated-text-using-amazon-translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eControl formality in machine translated text using Amazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e” To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/customizing-translations.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eon language translation formality\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-10-05T21:44:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/amazon-translate-formality-customization-support-dutch-korean-mexican-spanish/","postDateTime":"2022-10-05T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now adds formality customization support for Dutch, Korean, and Mexican Spanish","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are adding formality customization support for Dutch, Korean, and Mexican Spanish. We are also adding support for asynchronous batch translation. Now you can customize the formality of your translated output to suit your communication needs. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-02-amazon-translate-formality-customization","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/02/amazon-translate-formality-customization/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:50:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:11:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is\u0026nbsp;a\u0026nbsp;neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are introducing formality customization. This feature allows you to customize the level of formality in your translation output for six target languages - French, German, Hindi, Italian, Japanese, and Spanish. Now you can customize the formality of your translated output to suit your communication needs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Translate’s formality customization, customers have three options to control the level of formality in the output. The default option is no control over formality by letting the neural machine translation operate with no influence. Formal option is useful for customers, such as those in insurance and healthcare industry, who prefer a more formal machine translate output. Informal option is useful for customers, such as those in gaming and social media who prefer an informal machine translation output. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFormality customization is now available in the real-time operations in commercial \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Translate is available. For step-by-step instructions on how to customize the formality of your translation output, read our blog “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/control-formality-in-machine-translated-text-using-amazon-translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eControl formality in machine translated text using Amazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e” To learn more, please read the Amazon Translate documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/customizing-translations.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eon language translation formality\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-02-23T21:12:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/02/amazon-translate-formality-customization/","postDateTime":"2022-02-23T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now supports formality customization for French, German, Hindi, Italian, Japanese, and Spanish ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is\u0026nbsp;a\u0026nbsp;neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are introducing formality customization. This feature allows you to customize the level of formality in your translation output for six target languages - French, German, Hindi, Italian, Japanese, and Spanish. Now you can customize the formality of your translated output to suit your communication needs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-amazon-chime-sdk-meetings-aws-govcloud-us-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-chime-sdk-meetings-aws-govcloud-us-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:15:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/chime/chime-sdk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Chime SDK\u003c/a\u003e lets developers\u0026nbsp;add real-time audio, video, and screen share to their web and mobile applications with one-to-one and group meetings.  Amazon Chime SDK meetings are now available in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.  The expansion into the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions allows U.S. government agencies and contractors to move workloads into the cloud while addressing their specific regulatory and compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eEach AWS GovCloud (US) Region now includes an API endpoint which can create Amazon Chime SDK meetings in either AWS GovCloud (US) Region.  Developers can optimize their user’s experience by creating meetings in whichever AWS GovCloud (US) Region is nearest to their users, using the API endpoint in the same AWS GovCloud (US) Region as their application.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Chime SDK meetings or AWS GovCloud (US), refer to the following resources:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/chime/chime-sdk/features/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Chime SDK\u0026nbsp;features\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/chime/chime-sdk/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing information\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/chime/latest/dg/chime-sdk-meetings-regions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMeeting Regions\u003c/a\u003e in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/chime/latest/dg/what-is-chime.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Chime SDK Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-06T21:58:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-chime-sdk-meetings-aws-govcloud-us-regions/","postDateTime":"2022-01-05T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Chime SDK meetings now available in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/chime/chime-sdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Chime SDK\u003c/a\u003e lets developers\u0026nbsp;add real-time audio, video, and screen share to their web and mobile applications with one-to-one and group meetings.  Amazon Chime SDK meetings are now available in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.  The expansion into the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions allows U.S. government agencies and contractors to move workloads into the cloud while addressing their specific regulatory and compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#business-productivity","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"business-productivity","description":"marketing:marchitecture/business-productivity","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-chime-sdk","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-chime-sdk","description":"general:products/amazon-chime-sdk","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:51+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-chime","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-chime","description":"general:products/amazon-chime","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:37+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-transcribe","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-transcribe","description":"general:products/amazon-transcribe","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-12-amazon-translate-profanity-masking","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/12/amazon-translate-profanity-masking/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:32:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a\u0026nbsp;neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Starting today, you have the ability to mask commonly understood profane terms and prevent them from appearing in your translations. By default, Amazon Translate chooses clean words for your translation output. In cases where profane words appear in the translated output, you can now choose to mask the profane words and phrases with a grawlix string “?$#@$”. This 5-character sequence is used for each profane word or phrase, regardless of the length or number of characters.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eProfanity masking can be applied to both real-time and asynchronous batch translation jobs in all commercial AWS regions where Amazon Translate is available.\u0026nbsp;To learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/customizing-translations-profanity.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation on profanity masking\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-12-20T21:14:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/12/amazon-translate-profanity-masking/","postDateTime":"2021-12-20T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate announces profanity masking","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a\u0026nbsp;neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Starting today, you have the ability to mask commonly understood profane terms and prevent them from appearing in your translations. By default, Amazon Translate chooses clean words for your translation output. In cases where profane words appear in the translated output, you can now choose to mask the profane words and phrases with a grawlix string “?$#@$”. This 5-character sequence is used for each profane word or phrase, regardless of the length or number of characters.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-aws-privatelink-amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-privatelink-amazon-translate/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:36:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:05:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Amazon Translate now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpc/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)\u003c/a\u003e endpoints via AWS PrivateLink so you can securely initiate API calls to Amazon Translate from within your VPC and without using public IPs. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e provides private connectivity between VPCs and AWS services, without ever leaving the Amazon network, significantly simplifying your internal network architecture. You no longer need to use an Internet Gateway, Network Address Translation (NAT) devices or firewall proxies to connect to Amazon Translate.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eUsing AWS PrivateLink enables you to privately access Amazon Translate APIs from your VPC in a scalable manner by using interface VPC endpoints. A VPC endpoint is an elastic network interface in your subnet with a private IP address that serves as the entry point for all Amazon Translate API calls.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS PrivateLink support for Amazon Translate is now available in all commercial \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e. To\u0026nbsp;learn more, please see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-24T21:53:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-privatelink-amazon-translate/","postDateTime":"2021-11-24T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing AWS PrivateLink Support for Amazon Translate","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Amazon Translate now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/vpc.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)\u003c/a\u003e endpoints via AWS PrivateLink so you can securely initiate API calls to Amazon Translate from within your VPC and without using public IPs. \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/privatelink.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e provides private connectivity between VPCs and AWS services, without ever leaving the Amazon network, significantly simplifying your internal network architecture. You no longer need to use an Internet Gateway, Network Address Translation (NAT) devices or firewall proxies to connect to Amazon Translate.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-vpc","description":"general:products/amazon-vpc","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-amazon-translate-active-custom-translation-language-combinations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-translate-active-custom-translation-language-combinations/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:44:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:13:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are excited to announce the general availability of Active Custom Translation (ACT) to customize your translation between any \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecurrently supported languages\u003c/a\u003e. For example, you can now use ACT between German and French.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eACT produces custom-translated output without the need to build and maintain a custom translation model. With other custom translation products, customers can spend a lot of time and money on overhead expenses to manage and maintain various instances of both the customer data and the custom translation model for each language pair. With ACT, Amazon Translate will use your preferred translation examples as parallel data (PD) to customize the translation output. You can update your PD as often as needed to improve the translation quality without having to worry about retraining or managing custom translation models. Currently, ACT is available in the Europe West (Ireland), US East (Northern Virginia), and US West (Oregon) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can find step-by-step instructions in this “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/customizing-your-machine-translation-using-amazon-translate-active-custom-translation/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHow to use Amazon Translate’s Active Custom Translation\u003c/a\u003e” post. For more information on Amazon Translate ACT, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/customizing-translations-parallel-data.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-16T18:02:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-translate-active-custom-translation-language-combinations/","postDateTime":"2021-11-16T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Now Extends Support for Active Custom Translation to all language pair combinations","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are excited to announce the general availability of Active Custom Translation (ACT) to customize your translation between any \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecurrently supported languages\u003c/a\u003e. For example, you can now use ACT between German and French.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-amazon-translate-enables-multidirectional-custom-terminology","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-translate-enables-multidirectional-custom-terminology/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:51:04+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are introducing multidirectional custom terminology, to give you more control and flexibility over your translation workflows. Custom terminology is a feature of Amazon Translate that enables you to customize your translation of named entities such that your brand names, character names, model names, and other unique content using your terminology file. With multidirectional custom terminology, you no longer have to constrain yourself to set the first column of your terminology file as your source language. You will be now able to use the same terminology file to translate both to and from a specific language.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started review our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/how-custom-terminology.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecustomer terminology documentation page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;You can use AWS CLI, AWS Management Console, or supported SDK to create your customer terminology. You can upload your terminology file using the AWS CLI, Management Console, or supported SDKs. While creating a custom terminology you can specify whether you want it to be unidirectional or multidirectional. If you create a multidirectional custom terminology, you no longer have to constrain yourself to set the first column of your terminology file as your source language. You will be now able to use the same terminology file to translate both to and from a specific language. When a custom terminology is used as part of the translation request, the engine scans the terminology file before returning the final result. When the engine identifies an exact match between a terminology entry and a string in the source text, it locates the appropriate string in the proposed translation and replaces it with the terminology entry.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eMulti-directional Custom Terminology is now available in commercial AWS regions in both real-time and asynchronous batch translation operations . For step by step instructions to enable multidirectional custom terminology, read\u0026nbsp;our \u0026quot;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/customize-amazon-translate-output-to-meet-your-domain-and-organization-specific-vocabulary/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehow to blog\u0026quot; here\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;To learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e to get started, particularly read the documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/how-custom-terminology.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCustom Terminology\u003c/a\u003e and for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-11T23:02:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-translate-enables-multidirectional-custom-terminology/","postDateTime":"2021-11-11T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now enables multidirectional custom terminology","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Today, we are introducing multidirectional custom terminology, to give you more control and flexibility over your translation workflows. Custom terminology is a feature of Amazon Translate that enables you to customize your translation of named entities such that your brand names, character names, model names, and other unique content using your terminology file. With multidirectional custom terminology, you no longer have to constrain yourself to set the first column of your terminology file as your source language. You will be now able to use the same terminology file to translate both to and from a specific language.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-amazon-translate-supports-aws-kms-encryption","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-translate-supports-aws-kms-encryption/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:04:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Starting today, you can use your own encryption keys from the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kms/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Key Management Service (KMS)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to encrypt data placed in your S3 bucket. Up until now, Amazon Translate used Amazon S3-SSE to encrypt your data. AWS KMS makes it easy for you to create and manage keys, while controlling the use of encryption across a wide range of AWS services and in your applications. AWS KMS is a secure and resilient service that uses FIPS 140-2 validated hardware security modules to protect your keys. AWS KMS is integrated with AWS CloudTrail to provide you with logs of all key usage to help meet your regulatory and compliance needs. The feature can be configured via the AWS Management console or SDK and supports Amazon Translate’s asynchronous batch translation jobs.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eBatch Translation is now available in seven AWS regions - US East 1 (Northern Virginia), US East 2 (Ohio), US West 2 (Oregon), EU West 1 (Ireland), EU West 2 (London), EU Central 1 (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific North East 2 (Seoul).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor step by step instructions to run batch translation job, read our blog - \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/translating-documents-spreadsheets-and-presentations-in-office-open-xml-format-using-amazon-translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026quot;Translating documents, spreadsheets, and presentations in Office Open XML format using Amazon Translate.\u0026quot;\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;For information\u003cspan\u003e\u0026nbsp;visit \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" style\u003d\"background-color: rgb(255,255,255);\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-05T21:20:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-translate-supports-aws-kms-encryption/","postDateTime":"2021-11-05T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now supports AWS KMS Encryption","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high quality, affordable, and customizable language translation. Starting today, you can use your own encryption keys from the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kms.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Key Management Service (KMS)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to encrypt data placed in your S3 bucket. Up until now, Amazon Translate used Amazon S3-SSE to encrypt your data. AWS KMS makes it easy for you to create and manage keys, while controlling the use of encryption across a wide range of AWS services and in your applications. AWS KMS is a secure and resilient service that uses FIPS 140-2 validated hardware security modules to protect your keys. AWS KMS is integrated with AWS CloudTrail to provide you with logs of all key usage to help meet your regulatory and compliance needs. The feature can be configured via the AWS Management console or SDK and supports Amazon Translate’s asynchronous batch translation jobs.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-06-amazon-translate-now-supports-xml-localization-interchange-file-format-xliff-documents","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/amazon-translate-now-supports-xml-localization-interchange-file-format-xliff-documents/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:14:36+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation in 71 languages and variants –now supports translation of XML Localization Interchange File Format – XLIFF documents. Starting today, customers can submit their XLIFF documents for batch processing by Amazon Translate. Amazon Translate only translates sections where the target segment is empty. If the target section contains non-empty strings or pre-translated strings, Amazon Translate will not modify or overwrite the translation. You only pay for what you translate. This feature allows customers to continue using Translation Memory to translate content prior to machine translation and keep the machine translation costs low.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eBatch Translation is now available in seven regions - US East 1 (Northern Virginia), US East 2 (Ohio), US West 2 (Oregon), EU West 1 (Ireland), EU West 2 (London), EU Central 1 (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific North East 2 (Seoul). \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eRead the “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/translating-documents-spreadsheets-and-presentations-in-office-open-xml-format-using-amazon-translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTranslating documents, spreadsheets, and presentations in Office Open XML format using Amazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e” post for step by step instruction on translating document using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/#batch-translation\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e. For more information on how to use Batch Translation on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-06-23T18:17:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/amazon-translate-now-supports-xml-localization-interchange-file-format-xliff-documents/","postDateTime":"2021-06-23T11:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now supports XML Localization Interchange File Format - XLIFF documents","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation in 71 languages and variants –now supports translation of XML Localization Interchange File Format – XLIFF documents. Starting today, customers can submit their XLIFF documents for batch processing by Amazon Translate. Amazon Translate only translates sections where the target segment is empty. If the target section contains non-empty strings or pre-translated strings, Amazon Translate will not modify or overwrite the translation. You only pay for what you translate. This feature allows customers to continue using Translation Memory to translate content prior to machine translation and keep the machine translation costs low.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-06-amazon-translate-now-integrated-with-amazon-cloudwatch-events-amazon-eventbridge","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/amazon-translate-now-integrated-with-amazon-cloudwatch-events-amazon-eventbridge/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:18:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation in 71 languages and variants – is now integrated with Amazon CloudWatch Events and Amazon EventBridge. Starting today, you can use CloudWatch events to monitor the progress and completion of your Batch Translation jobs.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Events delivers a near real-time stream of system events that describes changes in AWS resources. You can create rules for CloudWatch Events and EventBridge, and events that match these rules will be routed to targets for processing. With this integration, you can receive a notification when your translation job is completed instead of manually requesting a status update.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EventBridge and Amazon CloudWatch Events are available for use with Amazon Translate at no additional charge.\u0026nbsp;Charges for other Amazon services (for example, Amazon S3) may apply. Both integrations are available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e that support Amazon Translate.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-06-15T15:38:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/amazon-translate-now-integrated-with-amazon-cloudwatch-events-amazon-eventbridge/","postDateTime":"2021-06-15T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate is Now Integrated with Amazon CloudWatch Events and Amazon EventBridge","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, affordable, and customizable language translation in 71 languages and variants – is now integrated with Amazon CloudWatch Events and Amazon EventBridge. Starting today, you can use CloudWatch events to monitor the progress and completion of your Batch Translation jobs.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-amazon-translate-increases-the-concurrent-api-limit-for-batch-translation-to-1000","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/amazon-translate-increases-the-concurrent-api-limit-for-batch-translation-to-1000/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a fully managed \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eneural machine translation service\u003c/a\u003e that delivers real-time, high-quality, affordable and customizable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate has increased the concurrent API limits for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ebatch translation jobs\u003c/a\u003e from 10 to 1000.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAsynchronous batch operations are particularly useful \u003cspan style\u003d\"\"\u003efor translating large collections of docx, xlsx, pptx, html, xml, and text files stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) with one API call. Now customers can submit up to 1000 jobs into the queue without being concerned about throttling\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eBatch Translation is available in seven regions - US East 1 (Northern Virginia), US East 2 (Ohio), US West 2 (Oregon), EU West 1 (Ireland), EU West 2 (London), EU Central 1 (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific North East 2 (Seoul).\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eRead the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs, particularly read the documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAsynchronous batch processing\u003c/a\u003e and get started on Batch Translation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-04T21:17:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/amazon-translate-increases-the-concurrent-api-limit-for-batch-translation-to-1000/","postDateTime":"2021-05-04T18:42:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate increases the concurrent API limit for Batch Translation to 1000","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a fully managed \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eneural machine translation service\u003c/a\u003e that delivers real-time, high-quality, affordable and customizable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate has increased the concurrent API limits for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ebatch translation jobs\u003c/a\u003e from 10 to 1000.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-04-amazon-translate-increases-the-size-limit-of-parallel-datafrom-1gb-to-5gb","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-translate-increases-the-size-limit-of-parallel-datafrom-1gb-to-5gb/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed, neural machine translation service that delivers real-time, high-quality, affordable and customizable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate has increased the size limit of parallel data (PD) from 1 GB to 5 GB. PD is used in Active Custom Translation (ACT), a feature that gives you more control over your machine translation output. You create PD by simply providing your translation examples in TMX, TSV, or CSV format. Then Amazon Translate uses your PD along with your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ebatch translation job\u003c/a\u003e to customize the translation output at runtime. With the increase in PD size, you can use more data to customize your ACT output.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eACT is available in Europe West (Ireland), US East (Northern Virginia), and US West (Oregon). You can find step-by-step instructions in this “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/customizing-your-machine-translation-using-amazon-translate-active-custom-translation/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eHow to use Amazon Translate’s Active Custom Translation\u003c/a\u003e” post. For more information on Amazon Translate ACT, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/customizing-translations-parallel-data.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-04-26T21:39:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-translate-increases-the-size-limit-of-parallel-datafrom-1gb-to-5gb/","postDateTime":"2021-04-26T16:01:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate increases the size limit of Parallel data from 1GB to 5GB","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed, neural machine translation service that delivers real-time, high-quality, affordable and customizable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate has increased the size limit of parallel data (PD) from 1 GB to 5 GB. PD is used in Active Custom Translation (ACT), a feature that gives you more control over your machine translation output. You create PD by simply providing your translation examples in TMX, TSV, or CSV format. Then Amazon Translate uses your PD along with your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ebatch translation job\u003c/a\u003e to customize the translation output at runtime. With the increase in PD size, you can use more data to customize your ACT output.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-amazon-translate-allows-user-to-specify-a-part-of-the-text-to-not-be-translated-do-not-translate","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-translate-allows-user-to-specify-a-part-of-the-text-to-not-be-translated-do-not-translate/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:21:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, and affordable language translation in fifty-five languages – is now enabling you to tag content so that it isn’t translate. Now, customer can wrap the text that need not be translated in a HTML element span and set translate attribute to “no”. This is available for both real-time and asynchronous batch API. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-translate-now-enables-you-to-mark-content-to-not-get-translated/\"\u003eRead our blog\u003c/a\u003e for step by step instructions on the Do Not Translate feature using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/#batch-translation\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e. For more information using Amazon Translate visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-06T19:13:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-translate-allows-user-to-specify-a-part-of-the-text-to-not-be-translated-do-not-translate/","postDateTime":"2020-11-06T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate allows user to specify a part of the text to not be translated – Do Not Translate","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, and affordable language translation in fifty-five languages – is now enabling you to tag content so that it isn’t translate. Now, customer can wrap the text that need not be translated in a HTML element span and set translate attribute to “no”. This is available for both real-time and asynchronous batch API. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-08-aws-amazon-com-machine-learning-contact-center-intelligence","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/08/aws-amazon-com-machine-learning-contact-center-intelligence/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/contact-center-intelligence/\"\u003eAWS Contact Center Intelligence\u003c/a\u003e (CCI) solutions enable customers using contact center solutions to leverage off-the-shelf functionality powered by machine learning like text-to-speech, translation, enterprise search, chatbots, business intelligence, and language comprehension. AWS CCI solutions allow customers to gain greater efficiencies and deliver increasingly tailored customer experiences within their existing contact center platform—with no machine learning expertise required.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS CCI solutions are focused on three stages of the contact center workflow: Self-Service, Live Call Analytics \u0026amp; Agent Assist, and Post-Call Analytics, and are available through participating APN partners. AWS CCI solutions leverage AWS AI Services, such as Amazon Lex, Amazon Kendra, Amazon Transcribe, Amazon Translate, and Amazon Comprehend. Additional information can be found on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/machine-learning/contact-center-intelligence/\"\u003eAWS CCI landing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-08-18T22:44:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/08/aws-amazon-com-machine-learning-contact-center-intelligence/","postDateTime":"2020-08-18T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS announces Contact Center Intelligence solutions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/machine-learning/contact-center-intelligence.html\"\u003eAWS Contact Center Intelligence\u003c/a\u003e (CCI) solutions enable customers using contact center solutions to leverage off-the-shelf functionality powered by machine learning like text-to-speech, translation, enterprise search, chatbots, business intelligence, and language comprehension. AWS CCI solutions allow customers to gain greater efficiencies and deliver increasingly tailored customer experiences within their existing contact center platform—with no machine learning expertise required.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kendra","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kendra","description":"general:products/amazon-kendra","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-lex","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-lex","description":"general:products/amazon-lex","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-transcribe","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-transcribe","description":"general:products/amazon-transcribe","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-comprehend","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-comprehend","description":"general:products/amazon-comprehend","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-translate-now-supports-translation-of-office-open-xml-documents","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-translate-now-supports-translation-of-office-open-xml-documents/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:25:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, and affordable language translation in fifty-five languages – is now supporting translation of Office open XML documents in docx, pptx, and xlsx format. Amazon Translate also increased the file size limit for each document in Batch Translation from 1 MB to 20 MB. Starting today, customers have the option to translate a large collection of docx, pptx, xlsx, HTML and plain text documents stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) bucket using the new asynchronous Batch Translation service. This is in addition to the real-time (synchronous) translation service that is already available, giving you options that best fit your needs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBatch Translation is now available in seven regions - US East 1 (Northern Virginia), US East 2 (Ohio), US West 2 (Oregon), EU West 1 (Ireland), EU West 2 (London), EU Central 1 (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific North East 2 (Seoul).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur asynchronous Batch Translation service accepts a batch of up to 5 GB in size per API call with each document not exceeding 20 MB in size, number of characters in each document not exceeding 1 million, and the number of documents in the S3 bucket folder not exceeding 1 million per batch. See \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is-limits.html#limits\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGuidelines and Limits\u003c/a\u003e for more details. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRead \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-translate-now-supports-office-documents/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eour blog\u003c/a\u003e for step by step instruction on translating document using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/#batch-translation\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e, For more information using Batch Translation on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-29T21:23:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-translate-now-supports-translation-of-office-open-xml-documents/","postDateTime":"2020-07-29T12:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now supports translation of Office Open XML documents","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate – a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, and affordable language translation in fifty-five languages – is now supporting translation of Office open XML documents in docx, pptx, and xlsx format. Amazon Translate also increased the file size limit for each document in Batch Translation from 1 MB to 20 MB. Starting today, customers have the option to translate a large collection of docx, pptx, xlsx, HTML and plain text documents stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) bucket using the new asynchronous Batch Translation service. This is in addition to the real-time (synchronous) translation service that is already available, giving you options that best fit your needs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-amazon-translate-now-adds-support-for-mexican-spanish","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-translate-now-adds-support-for-mexican-spanish/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:02:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports Mexican Spanish.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is now available in 55 languages and variants, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for the full list. Try all the languages in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-01T19:09:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-translate-now-adds-support-for-mexican-spanish/","postDateTime":"2020-05-01T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now adds support for Mexican Spanish","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports Mexican Spanish.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-translate-batch-translation-is-now-available-in-europe-london","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-translate-batch-translation-is-now-available-in-europe-london/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:29:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e Batch Translation is now available in EU West 2 (London). Now, customers have the option to translate a large collection of text or HTML documents stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) bucket using the new asynchronous Batch Translation service in EU West 2 (London). This is in addition to the real-time (synchronous) translation service that is already available, giving you options that best fit your needs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/#batch-translation\"\u003eBatch Translation\u003c/a\u003e is now available in seven regions - US East 1 (Northern Virginia), US East 2 (Ohio), US West 2 (Oregon), EU West 1 (Ireland), EU West 2 (London), EU Central 1 (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific North East 2 (Seoul). Now, AWS customers can reach a wider set of users in many geographies that are increasingly expecting to consume media and interact with organizations in the language of their choice. For a full list of regions Amazon Translate supports, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eGlobal Infrastructure page\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAsynchronous batch operations are particularly useful for translating very large collection of texts or HTML documents with one API call, when the application doesn\u0027t need a real-time response.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur asynchronous Batch Translation service accepts a batch of up to 5 GB in size per API call with each document not exceeding 1 MB in size and the number of documents in the S3 bucket folder not exceeding 1 million per batch. See \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is-limits.html\"\u003eGuidelines and Limits\u003c/a\u003e for more details.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRead the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs, particularly read the documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\"\u003eAsynchronous batch processing\u003c/a\u003e and get started on Batch Translation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/#batch-translation\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-20T20:07:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-translate-batch-translation-is-now-available-in-europe-london/","postDateTime":"2020-04-20T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Batch Translation is Now Available in Europe (London)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e Batch Translation is now available in EU West 2 (London). Now, customers have the option to translate a large collection of text or HTML documents stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) bucket using the new asynchronous Batch Translation service in EU West 2 (London). This is in addition to the real-time (synchronous) translation service that is already available, giving you options that best fit your needs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-amazon-translate-introduces-batch-translation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-translate-introduces-batch-translation/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:04:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e –\u003cspan style\u003d\"mso-fareast-font-family: \u0026quot;Times New Roman\u0026quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;\"\u003e a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, and affordable language translation in fifty-four languages – is now introducing Batch Translation. Starting today, customers have the option to translate a large collection of text or HTML documents stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) bucket using the new asynchronous Batch Translation service. This is in addition to the real-time (synchronous) translation service that is already available, giving you options that best fit your needs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Batch Translation is now available in six regions - US East 1 (Northern Virginia), US East 2 (Ohio), US West 2 (Oregon), EU West 1 (Ireland), EU Central 1 (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific North East 2 (Seoul).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Asynchronous batch operations are particularly useful for translating very large collection of texts or HTML documents with one API call, when the application doesn\u0027t need a real-time response. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur asynchronous Batch Translation service accepts a batch of up to 5 GB in size per API call with each document not exceeding 1 MB in size and the number of documents in the S3 bucket folder not exceeding 1 million per batch. See \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is-limits.html\"\u003eGuidelines and Limits\u003c/a\u003e for more details.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRead the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs, particularly read the documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/async.html\"\u003eAsynchronous batch processing\u003c/a\u003e and get started on Batch Translation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-08T23:07:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-translate-introduces-batch-translation/","postDateTime":"2020-01-08T11:48:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate introduces Batch Translation ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e –\u003cspan style\u003d\"mso-fareast-font-family: \u0026quot;Times New Roman\u0026quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;\"\u003e a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers high-quality, and affordable language translation in fifty-four languages – is now introducing Batch Translation. Starting today, customers have the option to translate a large collection of text or HTML documents stored in a folder in Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3) bucket using the new asynchronous Batch Translation service. This is in addition to the real-time (synchronous) translation service that is already available, giving you options that best fit your needs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-transcribe-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-transcribe-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:49:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/transcribe/\"\u003eAmazon Transcribe\u003c/a\u003e is an automatic speech recognition (ASR) service that makes it easy for you to add speech-to-text capabilities to your applications. Starting today, Amazon Transcribe becomes available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US-East) Region.\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Transcribe enables organizations to increase the accessibility and discoverability of their audio and video content, serving a breadth of use cases. For instance, contact centers may transcribe recorded calls for downstream analysis to better understand key call drivers. Or a media house may want to generate automatic transcriptions for the purpose of subtitling video. Amazon Transcribe is available in both batch mode, while supporting a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/what-is-transcribe.html\"\u003evariety of languages\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Transcribe is now available in the following \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e: US East (N. Virginia), EU (Ireland), US West (N. California), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), US West (Oregon), South America (Sao Paulo), Asia Pacific (Sydney), China (Beijing), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), US East (Ohio), Canada (Central), EU (London), China (Ningxia), EU (Paris), AWS GovCloud (US), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), Middle East (Bahrain).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/what-is-transcribe.html\"\u003eAmazon Transcribe documentation page.\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-19T19:34:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-transcribe-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region/","postDateTime":"2019-12-19T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Transcribe is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/transcribe.html\"\u003eAmazon Transcribe\u003c/a\u003e is an automatic speech recognition (ASR) service that makes it easy for you to add speech-to-text capabilities to your applications. Starting today, Amazon Transcribe becomes available in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US-East) Region.\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-transcribe","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-transcribe","description":"general:products/amazon-transcribe","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-translate-adds-support-22-more-languages-and-dialects","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-translate-adds-support-22-more-languages-and-dialects/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:32:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers real-time, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports the following more languages and dialects - Afrikaans, Albanian, Amharic, Azerbaijani, Bengali, Bosnian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Dari, Estonian, Canadian French, Georgian, Hausa, Latvian, Pashto, Serbian, Slovak, Slovenian, Somali, Swahili, Tagalog, and Tamil.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is now available in 54 languages and dialects. With  this launch, and continuous quality improvements across existing  language pairs, we are adding 1817 new language pairs, for a total of  2804. For a full list, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e With the launch of these languages and new regions announced . AWS customers can reach a wider set of users in many geographies that are increasingly expecting to consume media and interact with organizations in the language of their choice. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry all the 54 languages in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e, or see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-25T23:58:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-translate-adds-support-22-more-languages-and-dialects/","postDateTime":"2019-11-25T10:42:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Now Adds Support for Twenty-two More Languages and Variants - Afrikaans, Albanian, Amharic, Azerbaijani, Bengali, Bosnian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Dari, Estonian, Canadian French, Georgian, Hausa, Latvian, Pashto, Serbian, Slovak, Slovenian, Somali, Swahili, Tagalog, and Tamil","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed neural machine translation service that delivers real-time, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports the following more languages and dialects - Afrikaans, Albanian, Amharic, Azerbaijani, Bengali, Bosnian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Dari, Estonian, Canadian French, Georgian, Hausa, Latvian, Pashto, Serbian, Slovak, Slovenian, Somali, Swahili, Tagalog, and Tamil.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-translate-available-six-new-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-translate-available-six-new-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:26:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate is now available in six new regions - US West (Northern California), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Europe (Stockholm), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Asia Pacific (Sydney).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the addition of 6 new regions Amazon Translate is becoming truly global with availability in a total of 17 regions. Customers in these 17 regions can now keep the data within their regions and experience lower latency when using Amazon Translate. For a full list of regions Amazon Translate supports, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eGlobal Infrastructure page\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate now supports 54 languages  in 17 regions. Now, AWS customers can reach a wider set of users in many geographies that are increasingly expecting to consume media and interact with organizations in the language of their choice. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse Amazon Translate from your machine translation needs. Please check out \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e, or read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-25T23:58:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-translate-available-six-new-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-11-25T10:37:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate is Now Available in Six New Regions- US West (Northern California), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Europe (Stockholm), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Asia Pacific (Sydney)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate is now available in six new regions - US West (Northern California), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Europe (Stockholm), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Asia Pacific (Sydney).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-aws-for-wordpress-plugin-now-available-and-with-new-amazon-cloudfront-workflow","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/aws-for-wordpress-plugin-now-available-and-with-new-amazon-cloudfront-workflow/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:17:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Web Services announces the general availability of the AWS for WordPress plugin. Previously known as the Amazon Polly and Amazon AI plugin, the new AWS for WordPress plugin now provides a workflow to configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution that is highly optimized for WordPress websites.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon CloudFront, AWS’s content delivery network, accelerates the performance of your website by using a global network of 200 edge locations to cache and deliver content closer to your viewers. The plugin’s new CloudFront workflow creates a distribution with multiple cache behaviors, each one tailored to serving varying types of content for the best viewer and administrator experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/amazon-polly/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS for WordPress plugin is free to download\u003c/a\u003e from the WordPress Plugin Directory; standard charges apply for using AWS services. Existing users of the plugin who want to use the new CloudFront workflow will need to update the IAM policy for their plugin’s IAM user. Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/WordPressPlugIn.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eCloudFront Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e for more information about creating an updated IAM policy using the new managed IAM policy named \u003ci\u003eAWSforWordPressPluginPolicy\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRead our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/accelerating-wordpress-with-cloudfront-using-the-aws-for-wordpress-plugin/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e for a detailed guide to self-hosting WordPress with AWS and using the new CloudFront workflow within the plugin. Also read our newly updated whitepaper, “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://d1.awsstatic.com/whitepapers/wordpress-best-practices-on-aws.pdf\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eWordPress: Best Practices on AWS\u003c/a\u003e”, for more information about creating highly-scalable WordPress websites on AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-30T17:17:23Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/aws-for-wordpress-plugin-now-available-and-with-new-amazon-cloudfront-workflow/","postDateTime":"2019-10-30T17:08:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS for WordPress plugin now available and with new Amazon CloudFront workflow","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Web Services announces the general availability of the AWS for WordPress plugin. Previously known as the Amazon Polly and Amazon AI plugin, the new AWS for WordPress plugin now provides a workflow to configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution that is highly optimized for WordPress websites.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudfront","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudfront","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudfront","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:57+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-polly","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-polly","description":"general:products/amazon-polly","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-translate-adds-support-seven-new-languages","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-translate-adds-support-seven-new-languages/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed neural-network based machine translation service that delivers high-quality, real-time, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports Greek, Romanian, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Vietnamese, Thai, and Urdu.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese languages expand upon the existing 25 languages already available in Amazon Translate. With the new languages and quality improvements across many others, we are adding 392 new language pairs, for a total of 987. For a full list, see the Amazon Translate \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the launch of these languages AWS customers can reach a wider set of users that are increasingly expecting to consume media and interact with organizations in the language of their choice. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry the new set of languages in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e, or see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-translate-adds-support-seven-new-languages/","postDateTime":"2019-10-03T12:08:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now adds support for seven new languages - Greek, Romanian, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Vietnamese, Thai, and Urdu","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed neural-network based machine translation service that delivers high-quality, real-time, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports Greek, Romanian, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Vietnamese, Thai, and Urdu.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-07-introducing-ai-driven-social-media-dashboard","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/introducing-ai-driven-social-media-dashboard/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:12:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:41:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/ai-driven-social-media-dashboard/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAI-Driven Social Media Dashboard\u003c/a\u003e is a solution that monitors and ingests specified tweets using stream processing and leverages a serverless architecture and machine learning services to translate and extract insights from those tweets. The solution is easy to deploy and contains a data lake you can use to quickly and easily perform additional analytics on tweet data.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe solution uses \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ec2/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EC2\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpc/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon VPC\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon S3\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/lambda/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Lambda\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/comprehend/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Comprehend\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/glue/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Glue\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/athena/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Athena\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/quicksight/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon QuickSight\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about the AI-Driven Social Media Dashboard solution, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/ai-driven-social-media-dashboard/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esolution webpage\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional AWS Solutions offerings are available on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Solutions webpage\u003c/a\u003e,  where customers can browse solutions by product category or industry to  find AWS-vetted, automated, turnkey reference implementations that  address specific business needs.\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:49Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/introducing-ai-driven-social-media-dashboard/","postDateTime":"2019-07-22T15:39:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing AI-Driven Social Media Dashboard","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/ai-driven-social-media-dashboard.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAI-Driven Social Media Dashboard\u003c/a\u003e is a solution that monitors and ingests specified tweets using stream processing and leverages a serverless architecture and machine learning services to translate and extract insights from those tweets. The solution is easy to deploy and contains a data lake you can use to quickly and easily perform additional analytics on tweet data.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-solution","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-solution","description":"general:products/aws-solution","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-comprehend","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-comprehend","description":"general:products/amazon-comprehend","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-amazon-translate-available-mumbai-singapore-tokyo-canadacentral","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon-translate-available-mumbai-singapore-tokyo-canadacentral/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation is a form of language translation automation that uses deep learning models to deliver more accurate translation than traditional statistical and rule-based translation algorithms.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy using the service in Mumbai (India), Singapore, Tokyo (Japan), and Canada (Central), customers in those countries can now keep their data within their regions, and experience lower latency when using Amazon Translate. For a full list of regions Amazon Translate supports, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eGlobal Infrastructure page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate currently offers translation between 595 language pairs (e.g., French to German) across 25 languages. For a full list, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e. Try them out on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/console/\"\u003eAmazon Translate Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon-translate-available-mumbai-singapore-tokyo-canadacentral/","postDateTime":"2019-05-09T15:31:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate is now available in the Mumbai, Singapore, Tokyo, and Canada (Central) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation is a form of language translation automation that uses deep learning models to deliver more accurate translation than traditional statistical and rule-based translation algorithms.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-amazon-translate-support-hindi-farsi-malay-norwegian","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_translate_support_hindi_farsi_malay_norwegian/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:39+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed neural-network based machine translation service that delivers high-quality, real-time, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports Hindi, Farsi, Malay, and Norwegian.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese languages expand upon the existing 21 languages already available in Amazon Translate. With the new languages and quality improvements across many others, we are adding 178 new language pairs, for a total of 595. For a full list, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the launch of these languages AWS customers can reach a wider set of users that are increasingly expecting to consume media and interact with organizations in the language of their choice.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry the new set of languages in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate console\u003c/a\u003e, or see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_translate_support_hindi_farsi_malay_norwegian/","postDateTime":"2019-05-06T16:17:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Adds Support for Hindi, Farsi, Malay, and Norwegian","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/translate.html\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed neural-network based machine translation service that delivers high-quality, real-time, and affordable language translation. Today, we are announcing that Amazon Translate now supports Hindi, Farsi, Malay, and Norwegian.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:marchitecture/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:26:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-translate-is-now-available-in-the-aws-europe-frankfurt-and-asia-pacific-seoul-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-translate-is-now-available-in-the-aws-europe-frankfurt-and-asia-pacific-seoul-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:21:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation is a form of language translation automation that uses deep learning models to deliver more accurate translation than traditional statistical and rule-based translation algorithms.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy using the service in the Frankfurt and Seoul AWS regions, customers can now keep their data in Germany and Korea, and experience lower latency when using Amazon Translate. For a full list of regions Amazon Translate supports, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGlobal Infrastructure page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate currently offers translation between 417 language pairs (e.g., French to German) across 21 languages. For a full list, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e. Try them out on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/console/?nc1\u003df_m\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-translate-is-now-available-in-the-aws-europe-frankfurt-and-asia-pacific-seoul-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-02-28T13:33:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate is now available in the AWS Europe (Frankfurt) and Asia Pacific (Seoul) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation is a form of language translation automation that uses deep learning models to deliver more accurate translation than traditional statistical and rule-based translation algorithms.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-12-additional-ai-language-services-are-certified-as-pci-dss-compliant","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/additional-ai-language-services-are-certified-as-pci-dss-compliant/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:36:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Comprehend, Amazon Translate, and Amazon Transcribe are now certified as compliant with the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS), a proprietary information security standard administered by the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ePCI Security Standard Council\u003c/a\u003e. This means that these services are certified to handle cardholder data (CHD) and sensitive authentication data (SAD), including merchants, processors, acquirers, issuers, and service providers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor those of you who are not familiar with these services, please see quick summaries below:\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"margin-left: 40px;\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/comprehend/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Comprehend\u003c/a\u003e is a natural language processing (NLP) service that uses machine learning to find insights and relationships in text. To get started refer to this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/comprehend/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etechnical documentation\u003c/a\u003e, or check out this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/getting-started/tutorials/analyze-sentiment-comprehend/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e10-minute step-by-step tutorial\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"margin-left: 40px;\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural-network based machine translation service that delivers high-quality, real-time, and affordable language translation.\u0026nbsp;To get started refer to this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etechnical documentation\u003c/a\u003e, or check out this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/getting-started/tutorials/translate-text-between-languages-cloud/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e10-minute step-by-step tutorial\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"margin-left: 40px;\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/transcribe/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Transcribe\u003c/a\u003e is an automatic speech recognition (ASR) service that makes it easy for developers to add speech-to-text capability to their applications.\u0026nbsp;To get started refer to this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transcribe/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etechnical documentation\u003c/a\u003e, or check out this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/getting-started/tutorials/create-audio-transcript-transcribe/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e10-minute step-by-step tutorial\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to PCI DDS, all three services are also HIPAA eligible, enabling customers to use these services to build HIPAA-compliant applications or process documents containing protected health information (PHI).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a full list of services in scope for compliance programs, go to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/services-in-scope/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eServices in Scope by Compliance Program\u003c/a\u003e page.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:19Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/additional-ai-language-services-are-certified-as-pci-dss-compliant/","postDateTime":"2018-12-11T09:48:10Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Additional AI Language Services Are Certified as PCI DSS Compliant","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Comprehend, Amazon Translate, and Amazon Transcribe are now certified as compliant with the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS), a proprietary information security standard administered by the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ePCI Security Standard Council\u003c/a\u003e. This means that these services are certified to handle cardholder data (CHD) and sensitive authentication data (SAD), including merchants, processors, acquirers, issuers, and service providers.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-transcribe","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-transcribe","description":"general:products/amazon-transcribe","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-comprehend","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-comprehend","description":"general:products/amazon-comprehend","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-amazon-translate-now-supports-customized-translations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-translate-now-supports-customized-translations/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:58+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a fully managed neural-network based machine translation service that delivers high-quality, real-time, and affordable language translation. Today, we are introducing Custom Terminology, a feature that lets you customize Amazon Translate’s output to use company and domain-specific vocabulary. By uploading and invoking Custom Terminology with translation requests, you can ensure that your brand names, character names, model names, and other unique content get translated exactly the way you define it. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGet started with Custom Terminology by reviewing the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/how-custom-terminology.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation pages\u003c/a\u003e to understand the formatting requirements to ensure your files are readable. After that, you can create and upload your terminology using the AWS Console or supported SDKs. Once your terminology file is accepted, you can make translation requests to the service coupled with Custom Terminology. When matches are found, the translation results will automatically replace applicable content with terminology entries.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with Amazon Translate go to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetting Started with Amazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e or try this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/getting-started/tutorials/translate-text-between-languages-cloud/?trk\u003dgs_card\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e10-minute tutorial\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-translate-now-supports-customized-translations/","postDateTime":"2018-11-27T02:18:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Now Supports Customized Translations","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a fully managed neural-network based machine translation service that delivers high-quality, real-time, and affordable language translation. Today, we are introducing Custom Terminology, a feature that lets you customize Amazon Translate’s output to use company and domain-specific vocabulary. By uploading and invoking Custom Terminology with translation requests, you can ensure that your brand names, character names, model names, and other unique content get translated exactly the way you define it. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-amazon-translate-now-offers-113-new-language-pairs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/amazon-translate-now-offers-113-new-language-pairs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:50:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are launching 113 new language pairs. Customers can now translate between \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecurrently supported languages\u003c/a\u003e, such as French to Spanish for example, with a single API request. With this update, we are expanding the number of supported language pairs from 24 to 137. All supported language pairs are based on state-of-the-art neural machine translation algorithms. See the full list of supported language pairs on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/pairs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis documentation page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo use new language pairs, simply select any supported language pair in your API request or on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console Try Amazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e page. To get started with Amazon Translate go to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetting Started with Amazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e or check out this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/getting-started/tutorials/translate-text-between-languages-cloud/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e10-Minute step-by-step tutorial\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/amazon-translate-now-offers-113-new-language-pairs/","postDateTime":"2018-10-29T13:26:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate now offers 113 new language pairs ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Today, we are launching 113 new language pairs. Customers can now translate between \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecurrently supported languages\u003c/a\u003e, such as French to Spanish for example, with a single API request. With this update, we are expanding the number of supported language pairs from 24 to 137. All supported language pairs are based on state-of-the-art neural machine translation algorithms. See the full list of supported language pairs on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/pairs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis documentation page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-amazon-translate-achieves-hipaa-eligibility","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/amazon-translate-achieves-hipaa-eligibility/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. The Translate API is now an AWS HIPAA Eligible Service. If you have a Business Associate Addendum (BAA) in place with AWS, you can immediately start using Amazon Translate to translate texts containing protected health information (PHI). If you do not have a BAA in place with AWS or have any other questions about running HIPAA-regulated workloads on AWS, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/compliance-contact-us.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eplease contact us\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHIPAA Eligibility applies to all AWS Regions where Amazon Translate is available. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://d0.awsstatic.com/whitepapers/compliance/AWS_HIPAA_Compliance_Whitepaper.pdf\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eArchitecting for HIPAA Security and Compliance on Amazon Web Services Whitepaper\u003c/a\u003e for information and best practices about how to configure AWS HIPAA Eligible Services to store, process, and transmit PHI. To learn more about Amazon Translate, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:04Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/amazon-translate-achieves-hipaa-eligibility/","postDateTime":"2018-10-25T06:39:19Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Achieves HIPAA Eligibility","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. The Translate API is now an AWS HIPAA Eligible Service. If you have a Business Associate Addendum (BAA) in place with AWS, you can immediately start using Amazon Translate to translate texts containing protected health information (PHI). If you do not have a BAA in place with AWS or have any other questions about running HIPAA-regulated workloads on AWS, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/compliance-contact-us.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eplease contact us\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-amazon-translate-adds-six-new-languages","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-translate-adds-six-new-languages/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:53:15+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Starting today, Amazon Translate is adding the following six new languages that are highly requested by customers: Chinese (Traditional), Czech, Italian, Japanese, Russian, and Turkish. These languages expand upon the existing six languages already available in Amazon Translate: Arabic, Chinese (Simplified), French, German, Portuguese, and Spanish.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new set of languages expands the markets served by Amazon Translate to enable use cases such as real-time cross-lingual communication and on-demand translation of user-generated content to reach a broader global audience. For example, Japanese gaming developers can now implement cross-lingual real-time chat services using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.gamesparks.com/product/chat/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGameSparks Chat\u003c/a\u003e and Amazon Translate to remove language barriers among players.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition, six additional languages will be supported in the coming months: Danish, Dutch, Finnish, Hebrew, Polish, and Swedish.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry the new set of languages through the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e console, or visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information on Command Line Interface (CLI) and AWS SDKs. You can also read more about this feature on our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-translate-adds-support-for-new-languages\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Blog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:11Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-translate-adds-six-new-languages/","postDateTime":"2018-07-17T00:21:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate Adds Six New Languages","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Starting today, Amazon Translate is adding the following six new languages that are highly requested by customers: Chinese (Traditional), Czech, Italian, Japanese, Russian, and Turkish. These languages expand upon the existing six languages already available in Amazon Translate: Arabic, Chinese (Simplified), French, German, Portuguese, and Spanish.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-amazon-translate-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/amazon-translate-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:02:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation is a form of language translation automation that uses deep learning models to deliver more accurate translation than traditional statistical and rule-based translation algorithms. This service API is now available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Region\u003c/a\u003e, Amazon’s isolated cloud region built for sensitive data and regulated workloads.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this regional expansion, Amazon Translate can help U.S. government customers and government contractors better serve citizens by removing language barriers. Amazon Translate produces accurate translation at low-latency, which makes the service well suited for use cases that require real-time, on-demand translation of user-generated content, such as live chat for citizens with limited English proficiency. Also, Amazon Translate can be used to translate existing texts in a variety of languages for easier analysis. For example, public sector organizations can use the service to aggregate feedback provided by citizens who are more comfortable communicating in their native language.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Translate supports text to or from English to Arabic, Chinese (Simplified), French, German, Portuguese, and Spanish. Support for the following additional languages is coming soon: Chinese (Traditional), Czech, Italian, Japanese, Russian, and Turkish. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate product page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/amazon-translate-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-region/","postDateTime":"2018-06-20T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate is now Available in the AWS GovCloud (US) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation is a form of language translation automation that uses deep learning models to deliver more accurate translation than traditional statistical and rule-based translation algorithms. This service API is now available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Region\u003c/a\u003e, Amazon’s isolated cloud region built for sensitive data and regulated workloads.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-amazon-translate-is-now-supported-in-aws-mobile-sdk-for-android-and-ios","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/amazon-translate-is-now-supported-in-aws-mobile-sdk-for-android-and-ios/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:25:04+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Support for Amazon Translate API is now available in the AWS Mobile SDK for Android and iOS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, you can use the AWS Mobile SDK to develop and publish multilingual mobile apps quickly and easily with Amazon Translate. By adding real-time, on-demand translation, you can enable cross-lingual communications for common applications such as live chat, online reviews, and forum content.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Mobile SDK includes libraries, code samples, and documentation for iOS and Android. You can get started in minutes by downloading a zip file containing the SDKs. For more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/translate/latest/dg/get-started-sdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate Getting Started (SDK) documentation\u003c/a\u003e, GitHub page for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-android/tree/master/aws-android-sdk-translate\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAndroid\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-ios/tree/master/AWSTranslate\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eiOS\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/amazon-translate-is-now-supported-in-aws-mobile-sdk-for-android-and-ios/","postDateTime":"2018-05-25T11:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate is now supported in AWS Mobile SDK for Android and iOS","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Support for Amazon Translate API is now available in the AWS Mobile SDK for Android and iOS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-04-four-digital-courses-on-new-aws-services","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/04/four-digital-courses-on-new-AWS-services/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:48:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce the addition of four new free digital courses to our online training portfolio. These courses introduce security and machine learning services launched at April\u0027s AWS Summit in San Francisco.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e• \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.aws.training/learningobject/video?id\u003d19440\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eIntroduction to Amazon Certificate Manager Private Certificate Authority\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/a\u003e (ACM - PCA) discusses a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-certificate-manager-launches-private-certificate-authority/\"\u003enew feature\u003c/a\u003e that extends ACM’s certificate management capabilities to private certificates. You’ll learn how to get started with ACM - PCA, learn how this managed private CA service helps you easily and securely manage the lifecycle of your private certificates, and look at some use cases.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e• \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.aws.training/learningobject/video?id\u003d19441\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eIntroduction to AWS Secrets Manager\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/a\u003e provides a brief overview of how this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/secrets-manager/\"\u003enew service\u003c/a\u003e can help manage secrets like OAuth tokens and application API keys. It concludes with a demonstration of how AWS Secrets Manager can generate and automatically rotate your secrets and passwords.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e• \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.aws.training/learningobject/video?id\u003d19442\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eIntroduction to Amazon Translate\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/a\u003e discusses how this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003enew service\u003c/a\u003e uses advanced machine learning technologies to provide high quality translation on demand. The course introduces you to the features and benefits of the service. We also walk through several use cases and examples of Amazon Translate so you can see the service in action.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e• \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.aws.training/learningobject/video?id\u003d19443\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eIntroduction to Amazon Transcribe\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/a\u003e highlights key features and use cases of this new automatic speech recognition (ASR) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/transcribe/\"\u003eservice\u003c/a\u003e. We will review the benefits of deep learning to improve the accuracy of transcriptions and demonstrate a simple transcription.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can find these and other free digital training courses on AWS services at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.training\"\u003eaws.training\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/04/four-digital-courses-on-new-AWS-services/","postDateTime":"2018-04-13T13:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing 4 Free Digital Training Courses on New AWS Services","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce the addition of four new free digital courses to our online training portfolio. These courses introduce security and machine learning services launched at April\u0027s AWS Summit in San Francisco.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-secrets-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-secrets-manager","description":"general:products/aws-secrets-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-certificate-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-certificate-manager","description":"general:products/aws-certificate-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-transcribe","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-transcribe","description":"general:products/amazon-transcribe","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#training-and-certification","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"training-and-certification","description":"marketing:marchitecture/training-and-certification","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-04-amazon-translate-is-now-generally-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/04/amazon-translate-is-now-generally-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:24:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is now available for all customers. Powered by deep-learning technologies, Amazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Translate’s translation engines are trained on a wide variety of data across different domains to produce high-quality translations for various content. Currently, Amazon Translate supports translation between English and six major languages – Spanish, Chinese, French, German, Arabic, and Portuguese. Six additional languages will be supported in the coming months, including Japanese, Russian, Italian, Traditional Chinese, Turkish, and Czech. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With Amazon Translate, language is no longer a barrier to discovering information or connecting with each other. The service can automatically identify the source language when one is not formally specified. This helps to make Amazon Translate well suited for use cases that call for real-time, on-demand translation of user-generated content, such as live chat, online reviews, and forum content. You can also use Amazon Translate to enable language-independent processing, such as translating social media feeds into English for further data analysis across a multitude of languages. Whether it’s just a few words or even large batches of documents, Amazon Translate scales easily as your translation needs grow. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) regions. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate product page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:55:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/04/amazon-translate-is-now-generally-available/","postDateTime":"2018-04-04T23:37:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Translate is Now Generally Available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is now available for all customers. Powered by deep-learning technologies, Amazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-11-introducing-amazon-translate-now-in-preview","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/introducing-amazon-translate-now-in-preview/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:21+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation uses deep learning to deliver more accurate and more natural sounding translation than older statistical and rule-based translation algorithms. Amazon Translate enables translation at scale so that you can easily translate large volumes of text efficiently to handle tasks like localizing content for international users and facilitating real-time cross-lingual communication.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Transcribe is available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), and US West (Oregon) regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/translate/\"\u003eAmazon Translate\u003c/a\u003e home page and sign up for the Amazon Translate Preview.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:54:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/introducing-amazon-translate-now-in-preview/","postDateTime":"2017-11-29T15:10:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Translate – Now in Preview","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Translate is a neural machine translation service that delivers fast, high-quality, and affordable language translation. Neural machine translation uses deep learning to deliver more accurate and more natural sounding translation than older statistical and rule-based translation algorithms. Amazon Translate enables translation at scale so that you can easily translate large volumes of text efficiently to handle tasks like localizing content for international users and facilitating real-time cross-lingual communication.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-translate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-translate","description":"general:products/amazon-translate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:25+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":47,"totalHits":47},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}